# Sumra EMS — Complete Project Review

> **E**lection **M**anagement **S**ystem · Full-Stack · NestJS + React/Vite + PostgreSQL

---

## 1. What Is This Project?

A secure, role-based Election Management System where:
- **Admins** create elections, register constituencies, parties, and candidates, and control the election lifecycle.
- **Voters** log in, view candidates in their constituency, cast a single vote per election, and see results.

The tech stack was chosen for scalability and type-safety end-to-end:

| Layer | Technology | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Backend | **NestJS** (Node.js) | Opinionated, modular, TypeScript-first, great DI |
| ORM | **TypeORM** | Works natively with NestJS, supports PostgreSQL well |
| Database | **PostgreSQL** | Relational DB — perfect for elections with strict constraints |
| Auth | **JWT in HTTP-only cookies** | More secure than localStorage (immune to XSS) |
| Media | **Cloudinary** | Managed CDN for party logos and candidate photos |
| Frontend | **React + Vite + TypeScript** | Fast dev server, small bundle, modern React |
| Styling | **Tailwind CSS** | Utility-first, rapid UI development |

